the anechoic chamber is a test lab for  doing acoustic testing  it's a chamber within a chamber within a  chamber  that's steve i'm steve orfield the  founder of orfield laboratories in  minneapolis and we're talking about what  it feels like to sit in one of the  quietest rooms on earth  an anaconic chamber is a room that  absorbs sound  so it's quiet when we  put subjects in the anechoic chamber we  sit them in a chair and we turn off the  lights  it turns out that the only noises you'd  hear in there are noises that come from  inside your own body right away you'll  usually hear the sounds of your ears  buzzing  you'll start to hear the joints in your  arms and in your legs  like the sound of rubbing two pieces of  wood together  you'll clearly hear your heart beating  kind of a  boom  the flow of the air into your lungs  and sounds from inside your body that  you might have heard outside the chamber  are suddenly so much louder any noise  that would be startling outside the  chamber would be 16 times the startling  inside the chamber noises like your  stomach growling  or your knuckles cracking  people don't last that long inside  maybe an hour and 15 minutes and that's  mainly because of one of two reasons  some people find that very relaxing  and some people find that  fearful or claustrophobic  one person's peace and quiet is  another's personal nightmare
 

